{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","title":"prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":520,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:vertical-space]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties","line":861,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Smooth Horizontal--Vertical Splitting of a Vector Field]\n\\label{prop:horizontal-vector-field-properties}\n\n\\uses{def:submersion, def:vertical-space, def:horizontal-space, def:riemannian-metric, lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting, lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.25}\n\n\n\nEvery smooth vector field $W$ on $\\tilde M$ has a unique decomposition $W=W^H+W^V$ into smooth horizontal and vertical fields.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Pointwise set $W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi_xW_x)$ and $W_x^V=W_x-W_x^H$. The tangent-space splitting gives uniqueness and the horizontal-projection lemma gives smoothness of $W^H$; $W^V$ is then smooth.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Smooth Horizontal--Vertical Splitting of a Vector Field] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d766563746f722d6669656c642d70726f70657274696573\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asubmersion\">↗ def:submersion</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Avertical-space\">↗ def:vertical-space</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Atangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting\">↗ lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-projection-field-smooth\">↗ lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.25</span></span><p></p>Every smooth vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W$\">$W$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde M$\">$\\tilde M$</span> has a unique decomposition <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W=W^H+W^V$\">$W=W^H+W^V$</span> into smooth horizontal and vertical fields.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Pointwise set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi _xW_x)$\">$W_x^H=L_x(d\\pi _xW_x)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W_x^V=W_x-W_x^H$\">$W_x^V=W_x-W_x^H$</span>. The tangent-space splitting gives uniqueness and the horizontal-projection lemma gives smoothness of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W^H$\">$W^H$</span>; <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W^V$\">$W^V$</span> is then smooth. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:warped-products","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-along-map-smooth","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:submersion","title":"def:submersion","label":"def:submersion"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:vertical-space","title":"def:vertical-space","label":"def:vertical-space"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","label":"def:horizontal-space"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric","title":"def:riemannian-metric","label":"def:riemannian-metric"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting","title":"lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting","label":"lem:tangent-space-horizontal-vertical-splitting"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","title":"lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth","label":"lem:horizontal-projection-field-smooth"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter5#prob:riemannian-submersion-connection","title":"prob:riemannian-submersion-co